{
  "requirement": "Every {term}`requirements.sdk.graph.criteria.criterion` type implements\n`trust_but_verify::graph::Criterion<D>` for its\n{term}`requirements.sdk.application_domain`.\n\n```rust,ignore\npub trait Criterion<D: Domain>: Send + Sized {\n    type Ok: Serialize + DeserializeOwned + Send;\n\n    fn source_node_id(&self) -> NodeId<D>;\n    fn criterion_path(&self) -> CriterionPath;\n    fn version(&self) -> CriterionVersion;\n    fn execute(\n        self,\n        ctx: &mut ValidationContext<'_, D>,\n    ) -> impl Future<Output = Result<Self::Ok, ValidationError<D::Error>>> + Send;\n}\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The subject is a type-level contract. Every criterion type implements `Criterion<D>` for its application domain, with `Send + Sized`, an `Ok` that is `Serialize + DeserializeOwned + Send`, the four methods, and a `Send` future from `execute`. The compiler enforces the contract, and the reviewed tests exercise it through real implementations.\n\n- **Real implementations in several domains.** `impl Review/Criterion<Memory>` (in `crates/trust-but-verify/src/graph/validation_tests.rs` and `src/agent/tests.rs`) and `impl Review<O>/Criterion<Application>` (in `tests/contracts.rs`) implement every member. Other implementations are in `tests/storage.rs`, `src/agent/configured.rs` and `src/agent/project_sources.rs`. All are driven through the `Validator`, so the full trait shape is compiled and used.\n- **Source node and path.**\n  - `criteria_keep_typed_answers_and_persist_only_when_requested` asserts `source_node_id()` and `criterion_path()` on the verified value and on the loaded record.\n  - `deterministic_validation_uses_required_storage_without_an_agent` loads the record by node and an empty `CriterionPath`.\n- **Version.**\n  - `criteria_keep_typed_answers_and_persist_only_when_requested` asserts `version()` equals \"v1\".\n  - `caller_reuses_negative_answers_and_compares_revisions_explicitly` covers v1 vs v2 revisions and compatibility. It also covers a record with no stored version.\n  - Version has its own refining requirement.\n- **`execute` and its context.**\n  - `deterministic_validation_uses_required_storage_without_an_agent` runs `execute` with a `ValidationContext` and checks the result, the rationale and the recorded dependency.\n  - `criteria_keep_typed_answers_and_persist_only_when_requested` checks the answer, the execution count and the write count.\n- **`Ok` bounds.**\n  - Serialize and deserialize: `criteria_keep_typed_answers_and_persist_only_when_requested` stores and reloads `Assessment`, `Vec<String>` and `()`. It checks the stored JSON and the decoded output.\n  - `Send` without `Sync`: `validation_and_answer_need_send_without_sync` uses `Cell<u32>` as `Ok`. This would not compile if `Ok` required `Sync`.\n- **`Send` future.** `validation_and_answer_need_send_without_sync` passes the `verify`, `store_evidence`, `load_evidence` and `refresh_evidence` futures through the `send(...)` helper. This checks that the futures are `Send`, including the criterion's `execute` future.\n- **Public export.** `public_exports_match_the_appendix` checks that `Criterion` is exported at the documented path. It also checks that the shipping consumer compiles against it.\n\nI found no unexercised obligation. The tests are also marked with {test} references to the subject. I used the search only to confirm which criterion implementations exist.",
  "references": "a879f0ae49401bc00fac45ea5398c96091e5d5707b6490f80c3427a3894f1a04",
